# ENG-02: make line-ending handling explicit. Without this file the result
# depends on each contributor's core.autocrlf setting, which is what produced
# the recurring "LF will be replaced by CRLF" noise and the mojibake incidents
# in RELEASE.md and download/hls/engine.rs.
#
# Existing files are intentionally left alone: adding this file does not
# rewrite anything. Run `git add --renormalize .` only in a dedicated commit
# with a clean working tree.

* text=auto

# Shell scripts must keep LF even when checked out on Windows, otherwise
# git-bash, WSL and the Linux CI runners fail with "bad interpreter".
*.sh text eol=lf

# Source and config: store LF, let git convert on checkout.
*.rs text
*.ts text
*.tsx text
*.js text
*.mjs text
*.json text
*.css text
*.html text
*.md text
*.toml text
*.yml text
*.yaml text
*.sql text

# Binary assets: never convert line endings, never attempt a text diff.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.torrent binary

# Generated lockfile: still tracked, but excluded from diffs to keep reviews
# readable. Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT listed - dependency changes there
# must stay reviewable.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff
